    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d896">

                <pb facs="0818" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 850a.001/6.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 6, Luxemburg series.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 4, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith,
                    together with the office copy thereof, a letter<anchor n="1" xml:id="d896-f1"/>
                    addressed to the President of the United <pb facs="0819" n="703" xml:id="pg703"
                    /> States of America, which I have this day received from the Minister of State,
                    President of the Government of the Grand Duchy of Luxemburg, whereby her Royal
                    Highness the Grand Duchess, Regent of the Grand Duchy, notifies the President of
                    the United States of the decease of His Royal Highness the Grand Duke William,
                    and of the continuance of the Regency until the attainment of majority of Her
                    Royal Highness the Grand Duchess Marie Adelaide.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lloyd Bryce.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
